# Start a dev server in the background, use it to reproduce a failing
# integration test, fix the bug, and confirm no server survives past exit.
@real
@size 140x45
@fixture qa/fixtures/real/wf-devserver-debug
WAITFOR /describe a task/ 30
SHOT ready
TURN Start the dev server in the background on port 8089, then use it to figure out why TestHealthContentType in integration_test.go fails, and fix the bug. Run the test against the running server to confirm the fix, then leave the server running.
SHOT after-fix
SEND /bashes
WAIT 2
SHOT bashes
RUN cd {PROJ} && PORT=8089 go test ./... -run TestHealthContentType -v -count=1
RELAUNCH
WAITFOR /describe a task/ 30
SHOT relaunched
RUN ! (lsof -i :8089 -t 2>/dev/null | grep -q .)
NOTE kiln may or may not kill a background dev server on exit by design; the port-probe RUN above is the real check, not an assumption.
